 "conventions": "- Every position is from its parent's top left: the left or right page's drawable area, or the element it's in.\n    `x` from the left edge, `r` from the right edge (a TOPRIGHT anchor), `y` from the top, `b` from the bottom.\n  - A text's `y` is its line's top; the client puts a FontString of height `size` at y + (lineHeight - size) / 2.\n    `w` on a text is its width when it is cut (an ellipsis) or wraps.\n  - An ink names a face of BookArt.lua (print, italic, gilt, hand, handSemi, handBold), a size and a colour, and\n    `look` when BOARD_LOOK already has that colour. `caps`: capitals at 0.84 of the size (the client has no small\n    capitals), for the canvas's IM Fell English SC. `upper`: capitals at full size.",
